<title>USA: Air Ontario attendants ratify contract.</title>
<headline>Air Ontario attendants ratify contract.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Ontario, one of five Air Canada regional carriers, said a tentative agreement with its flight attendants was ratified on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Flight attendants, who were represented by the Canadian Union of Public Employees, would return to work on Wednesday and would operate all scheduled flights, the company said.</p>
<p>On April 6, the airline said it would resume flights from Toronto City Centre Airport to Ottowa, Montreal and London. The frequency of some flights on other routes would also be increased, it said.</p>
<p>Air Ontario provides service to 17 destinations throughout central Canada and the northeastern United States.</p>
<p>New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
